// =============================================================================
//  Washoi / SHAG Engine -- NetRadiant entity classes
// =============================================================================
//
//  Every class below was derived from the engine's own readers, not guessed:
//
//    SpawnPointTable.ts            info_player_*, team_CTF_*spawn
//    TriggerTable.ts               trigger_teleport, trigger_push + dest classes
//    LiftSystem.ts                 func_door, func_plat, func_button,
//                                  trigger_once, trigger_multiple
//    BombSiteTable.ts              team_CTF_*flag, trigger_capture_area,
//                                  misc_capture_area_indicator, target_explosion
//    PickupTable.ts                weapon_*, ammo_*, item_armor_*, item_health_*
//    MapAreaLightEntities.ts       light_area
//    MapGodRayEntities.ts          light_volumetric, sun lights
//    MapRenderer.ts (raw path)     misc_model, sprite*, npc_sprite, info_npc,
//                                  street_lamp, build_zone, info_debris_zone
//
//  Two entity paths exist and are NOT interchangeable (docs/reference/entities.md):
//    * compiled-BSP path  -- the FPS route. Everything in the first five
//                            sections below is read out of the .bsp entity lump.
//    * raw-.map path      -- editor / MapRenderer only, listed at the bottom.
//  Only BSP-path classes affect gameplay.
//
//  SHAG coordinate convention: the .map is Z-up Quake style, converted
//  X Y Z -> X Z Y on load. Author normally.
//
//  Engine quirks that will bite you, called out inline below:
//    * BRUSH triggers/movers have NO reliable "origin". LiftSystem computes
//      AABB = submodel AABB + origin, so the engine ADDS your origin to an
//      already-world-space box. Leave origin at "0 0 0" for func_door,
//      func_plat, func_button, trigger_once and trigger_multiple.
//      trigger_teleport / trigger_push use the submodel AABB directly and
//      ignore origin entirely.
//    * The engine honours only SURF_SKY (0x4), SURF_NODRAW (0x80) and
//      CONTENTS_DETAIL (0x8000000) from the BSP. nolightmap / nonsolid /
//      trans must be expressed in the .shader, not in brush face flags.
//    * SURF_HINT and SURF_SKIP are not filtered, so hint/skip brushes are
//      meshed like anything else. Keep them out unless you mean it.
//    * max 4 lightmap styles per surface (MAX_LIGHTMAPS). A surface needing
//      more will not render correctly, and a surface must not straddle a
//      lightmap page.
// =============================================================================

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  WORLD
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*QUAKED worldspawn (0 0 0) ?
  identity
  -------- KEYS --------
  message: Map Title
  --------
  light grid
  Must agree with "defaultGridSize" in makebspdata/washoi.json (64 64 128),
  otherwise the engine's grid origin is offset and dynamic model lighting
  drifts. Only override if you also change the profile.
  gridsize: Light Grid Size (default: 64 64 128)
  --------
  lighting / global ambience
  ambient: Macro Occlusion Ambient (default: 0)
  color: Global Ambient Color (default: 1 1 1)
  ambient_sky: Sky Ambient Color (default: 1 1 1)
  shading: Shading Mode (default: lambert)
  attenuation: Attenuation Model (default: standard)
  exposurefilter: Exposure Filter (default: reinhard)
  saturation: Saturation Multiplier (default: 1.25)
  saturationramp: Saturation Ramp (default: halfpower)
  cutoff: Light Cutoff (default: 0.1)
  fadeout: Light Fadeout (default: 0.0)
  backsplashspot: Spot Backsplash (default: 0.1)
  backsplashsurface: Surface Backsplash (default: 0.0)
  haloshader: Halo Shader (default: none)
  ambient_testradius: Ambient Test Radius (default: 512)
  ambient_gatheradius: Ambient Gather Radius (default: 256)
  grid_ambientbias: Grid Ambient Bias (default: 1.5)
  grid_directbias: Grid Direct Bias (default: 1.5)
  grid_smoothambient: Grid Smooth Ambient Radius (default: 256)
  grid_smoothambient_passes: Grid Smooth Ambient Passes (default: 4)
  grid_smoothdirect: Grid Smooth Direct Radius (default: 128)
  grid_smoothdirect_passes: Grid Smooth Direct Passes (default: 3)
  grid_minambient: Grid Min Ambient (default: 0)
  grid_maxambient: Grid Max Ambient (default: 0)
  _lightingIntensity: LDR Lightmap Intensity (default: 1.75)
  --------
  lightmaps / rendering passes
  samplesize: Lightmap Sample Size (default: 8)
  deluxe: Deluxe Mapping (default: 1)
  deluxe_minangle: Deluxe Min Angle (default: 15)
  supersample: Supersample Radius (default: 0)
  smooth: Lightmap Smooth Radius (default: 0.35)
  smoothpasses: Lightmap Smooth Passes (default: 4)
  antialiasing: AA Passes (default: 0)
  --------
  radiosity
  radiosity: Bounce Light Intensity (default: 1.0)
  rad_color_ratio: Bounce Color Ratio (default: 1.0)
  rad_interval: Bounce Interval (default: 4)
  rad_ao_intensity: Bounce AO Intensity (default: 0.5)
  rad_ao_min: Bounce AO Min (default: 0)
  rad_ao_max: Bounce AO Max (default: 32)
  --------
  SHAG engine specific
  Read by the engine, not by the compiler. God rays are driven by a
  "light" whose "target" names a marker entity (typically "sun" or
  "_sun"); the marker's origin sets the travel direction. Do NOT put
  q3map_sun / q3map_surfacelight in sky shaders -- the compiler already
  derives sky ambient from ambient_sky and they will double up.
  godrays: Enable God Rays (default: 0)
  godrays_color: God Ray Color (default: 1 1 1)
  _floodlight: Floodlight (default: 255 255 240 768 170)
*/

